      "text": "```python\n# The problem requires us to find the smallest positive integer that is both an integer power of 11 and is not a palindrome.\n# We will iterate through the powers of 11 starting from 11^1 and check each one to see if it is a palindrome.\n\ndef is_palindrome(n):\n    return str(n) == str(n)[::-1]\n\n# Start with the first power of 11\npower = 1\nnumber = 11 ** power\n\n# Iterate through the powers of 11\nwhile True:\n    if not is_palindrome(number):\n        break\n    power += 1\n    number = 11 ** power\n\nprint(number)\n```\n```output\n161051\n```\nThe smallest positive integer that is both an integer power of 11 and is not a palindrome is \\(\\boxed{161051}\\).",
